      ":question/id": "098da840-2ee3-511e-9a51-a46a65b8c410",
      ":question/problem": "Find the **exact** value of $\\cos\\left(75^\\circ\\right)$.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that*\n\n$$\n75^\\circ=45^\\circ+30^\\circ.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(x+y)=\\cos x\\cos y-\\sin x\\sin y.\n$$\n\nApply it to the decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(75^\\circ\\right)=\\cos\\left(45^\\circ+30^\\circ\\right).\n$$\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(45^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(30^\\circ\\right)-\\sin\\left(45^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(30^\\circ\\right)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed special-angle values and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\\n&=\\frac{- \\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6}}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
